Application Title: ClientHub (v5.0 Connected Commerce Edition)

Hosted Location: https://vinaybhagatd.github.io/vyapar-crm/


PART 1: PRIVACY POLICY & DATA PROTECTION NOTICE
1. Introduction & Architecture Overview
ClientHub ("the Application," "we," "us," or "our") operates as a Progressive Web Application (PWA) designed for field
sales automation, lead capture, and multi-channel marketing outreach.

ClientHub is designed around a Client-Side First / Local Storage Architecture. All lead metadata (names, phone numbers,
email addresses, SME niche categories, notes, and follow-up schedules) are stored and processed locally within your
device's web browser storage (localStorage and Web Cache). We do not operate a centralized cloud database that collects,
harvests, or sells your client or lead data.


2. Information We Process & How It Is Collected
A. User-Provided Data & Lead Records
• Lead CRM Data: Information manually entered, imported via CSV files, captured through voice recognition (Voice
Wizard), or extracted via optical character recognition (Visiting Card OCR Scanner).

• Communication Templates: Custom sales pitch scripts, outreach messages, and follow-up reminders created within the
Message Studio.

B. Hardware Permissions & Device Access
ClientHub requests real-time access to device hardware only when explicitly initiated by the user:


• Microphone Access (Voice Wizard): Used exclusively to transcribe spoken text into structured CRM input fields via the
browser’s native Web Speech API (webkitSpeechRecognition). Audio streams are processed in real-time and are never
recorded, stored, or transmitted to our servers.

• Camera Access & Photo Uploads (Visiting Card OCR Scanner): Used exclusively to capture or upload images of visiting
cards, brochures, or business documents. Images are processed locally on-device using Tesseract.js for optical text
extraction. Photos are not saved to any external remote server.

3. Regulatory Compliance: GDPR & DPDP Act
ClientHub strictly complies with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR - Regulation (EU) 2016/679) and the
Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDP Act 2023, India).


A. Lawful Basis for Processing
• Consent: Hardware permissions (Microphone, Camera) are granted explicitly by the user on a per-action basis.

• Legitimate Interest: Data processed within the CRM is strictly for the business execution purposes of the user.

B. Data Subject Rights
Users possess full control over their personal and client data under applicable data privacy laws:


• Right to Access & Data Portability: Users can export their entire lead database at any time into a standard,
machine-readable format using the Export CSV feature.

• Right to Erasure (Right to be Forgotten): Users can permanently delete individual lead records using the single-click
deletion button (deleteLead()) or clear all execution logs. Clearing browser storage removes all cached records
permanently.

• Right to Rectification: Users can edit and update any stored lead profile in real-time via the built-in Lead Editing
Interface.

4. Third-Party Libraries & External Links
ClientHub utilizes open-source content delivery networks (CDNs) for client-side rendering and UI processing:


• Tailwind CSS & FontAwesome: Loaded for interface styling and icon rendering.

• Alpine.js & Tesseract.js: Executed client-side for dynamic UI binding and optical character recognition.

• External Outreach Protocols: ClientHub generates standard https://web.whatsapp.com/ deep links and standard mailto:
mail links. Triggering these actions hands over processing to the respective third-party applications (WhatsApp / Native
Email Client) under their separate privacy policies.

5. Contact Information
For privacy inquiries, compliance disclosures, or legal requests regarding ClientHub, please direct communications to:


• Project Repository: https://vinaybhagatd.github.io/vyapar-crm/

